  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Ramachandrapuram?", answer: "Message IB Gram with the programme, subject, level and exam session. We then draw a shortlist for that exact course from tutors across India, since Konaseema has no IB school to supply local ones. You fix the lesson times afterwards, try a free lesson first, and can request a different tutor if the first pairing does not feel right." },
    { question: "Which IGCSE boards can you cover for a Ramachandrapuram student?", answer: "Both Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel. Matching follows the subject code and tier, such as Cambridge 0625 Physics or Edexcel 4BI1 Biology, and practice uses that board's own papers and mark schemes. Lessons are live and online, so a student here works with the same kind of specialist as a student in Hyderabad or Chennai." },
    { question: "Will a tutor visit our home in Ramachandrapuram?", answer: "No. Tutors do not visit homes in Ramachandrapuram, and in-person lessons exist only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. Your child gets private tuition at home through a laptop: a desk in your house, a tutor on live video and a shared screen for working problems. Be cautious about any promise of a doorstep visit." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost in Ramachandrapuram?", answer: "The fee depends on level, subject, the tutor's recent experience with that syllabus and the weekly hours, not on where in Ramachandrapuram you live. IB Higher Level subjects usually cost more than IGCSE Core because fewer tutors have taught them lately. The figure comes in writing before the free trial, with no travel charge and no long contract." },
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school near Ramachandrapuram?", answer: "None that we can confirm in the town. The nearest Cambridge-approved school is Laurel High Global School in Rajahmundry, about 35 kilometres away, which taught Cambridge Primary and Lower Secondary to Grade 8 at last check. IB Diploma and IGCSE campuses begin around Visakhapatnam and Hyderabad, so most families keep a child at school locally and add an online tutor." },
    { question: "Can a Telugu-medium child move to IGCSE or IB?", answer: "Yes, with a short bridge. Subject knowledge carries across, but papers are in English, so the first weeks go on technical vocabulary, command words and timed paragraphs. If you want a tutor who can also explain a stuck idea in Telugu or Hindi, say so when we match, and we will try to find one." },
    { question: "Will online lessons cope with cyclone-season power and internet cuts?", answer: "They can, with simple precautions. Charge the laptop before a forecast storm, keep a phone hotspot ready and test the connection from the room you will use. If an outage cuts a session, tell the tutor early so a replacement slot can be arranged. Students sitting November papers should start revision before the stormy weeks." },
    { question: "Is the first lesson really free?", answer: "Yes. Your child takes a real topic from their own syllabus with the proposed tutor on video and nothing is payable afterwards. A short plan for the first month follows, and you can accept it, ask for changes or request another tutor. Many Ramachandrapuram families book the trial for a Sunday morning, when the house is calm." },
    { question: "Will the tutor write my child's Internal Assessment or Extended Essay?", answer: "No, and any tutor who offers to is breaking IB academic integrity rules. IB Gram tutors coach: they help choose a question that can be researched, explain each criterion, suggest how to gather data and comment honestly on drafts the student has written. The submitted work stays entirely the student's own." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you cover for Ramachandrapuram students?", answer: "Requests cluster around Maths AA and AI at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science and Telugu or Hindi, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance as coaching. Less common subjects go through the same matching, with a smaller pool of tutors to choose from." },
    { question: "Can you help a child who is still in MYP or PYP?", answer: "Yes. For PYP the focus is reading, writing, number sense and research skills for the Exhibition. For MYP it is criterion-based analysis in sciences and languages and the Personal Project journal. These lessons suit children returning from an IB school elsewhere, or preparing for a move to one." },
    { question: "When should a Ramachandrapuram student start tutoring?", answer: "Ideally in the first term of the course, which means Class 9 for IGCSE or Class 11 for the IB Diploma. Early lessons repair shaky foundations before internal deadlines and predicted grades collide. A student who joins late still gains, with the work narrowed to the highest-value topics and built around timed papers." },
    { question: "Can lessons avoid Sankranti and other festival weeks?", answer: "Yes. We fit sessions around Bhogi, Sankranti and Kanuma, Dasara, Diwali and any family event. Most households choose weekday evenings or weekend mornings, and hot afternoons are avoided in summer. A second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is simple to add online." },
    { question: "How does IB or IGCSE fit with AP EAPCET or NEET?", answer: "Eligibility depends on the subjects studied and on equivalence of the board. AP EAPCET, NEET-UG and JEE Main publish their own notices, and students from IB or IGCSE backgrounds may need AIU equivalence and to meet local-status rules. Check the official notice for your exact course early and keep tutoring aimed at the depth those exams expect." },
    { question: "Can my child join an Andhra junior college after IGCSE?", answer: "Possibly, but it depends on the college and on board equivalence, so ask both before you commit. IGCSE is a Class 10 level qualification, and a junior college may want an equivalence certificate. Tutors cannot arrange admission, though they can prepare the student for the subject depth the next stage expects." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not a good fit?", answer: "Tell us and another tutor is found. Progress is reviewed with you every few weeks, and a re-match is available whenever the pairing is off, because a child should not sit through lessons that are not helping. No long contract binds you, so pausing or stopping also carries no penalty." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors chosen for Ramachandrapuram students?", answer: "Before any introduction a tutor is screened on qualifications, recent teaching of the exact subject and level, and skill with assessment criteria. Because Konaseema has no local specialist base, preference goes to tutors who taught the current syllabus recently. The free lesson then lets you test the fit yourself." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram linked to Laurel High Global School or any other school?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to, endorsement from or role at Laurel High Global School, any school named here, the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge University Press and Assessment or Pearson Edexcel. Schools are named only to show where confirmed options exist." }
  ],

